<title>USA: 3M says currency effects might trim '97 net.</title>
<headline>3M says currency effects might trim '97 net.</headline>
<dateline>ST. PAUL, Minn. 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Minnesota Mining &amp; Manufacturing Co said Tuesday that the impact of currency translations could reduce 1997 net income by up to $0.25 a share.  </p>
<p>3M earned $3.63 a share in 1996, up more than 12 percent over the prior year. Had the dollar stayed constant, that increase would have been 17 percent, said 3M Chairman and Chief Executive L.D. DeSimone at the company's annual meeting.</p>
<p>The First Call consensus forecast projects 3M's 1997 earnings at $4.11 a share.</p>
<p>		  ((Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8787))</p>
